# Rocci documentation

Rocci is a `.rocci` template language and runtime for Roc. You author HTML
components and HTTP handlers, Rocci lowers them to ordinary Roc, and Datastar
transports browser intent over the same local HTTP origin the preview window
uses.

This manual describes **development** `main`. Behavior is experimental; verify
commands against the source you built.

Rocdown is a separate Markdown-first product. It does not belong in this
learning path. Start at [Rocdown](/rocdown/) if you are writing documentation
sites instead of Rocci applications.

## What can I build?

Standalone `.rocci` apps, custom `main.roc` servers that reuse components, and
ad-hoc macOS desktop bundles around the same HTTP server. Durable state stays
on the server. The browser morphs HTML; it does not own the domain model.

:note[title: "Maturity"] {{
    macOS and Linux development are tested in CI. Windows development uses the
    system webview and is documented only to that level. Production signing,
    installers, and a versioned release channel are not the install path yet.
}}

